{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Sally on the Aegean Sea", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Sally in the Middle East", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > Out and About in the City > Istanbul", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 5, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn5le05ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Geographic Features / Building and Structures", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you travel, you often look at the geographic features of an area as well as the buildings and structures.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "All of those buildings were cut out of the rock!  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I went from Petra north to the Dead Sea. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Geographic Features\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"rose-colored sandstone <br> stone<br> rock walls<br> winding canyon <br> valley <br> sandstone<br> desert<br> dunes<br> sea\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "&nbsp;", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structures\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"building <br> residence<br> hospital<br> mosque<br> aqueduct<br> ruins<br> palace\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Comparatives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the comparative form to compare two things.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The comparative form ends in -er: <span class=\"italic\">taller</span>.<br> The word more is used with longer words: <span class=\"italic\">more beautiful</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use the comparative with a noun: <span class=\"italic\">a bigger car, his car was  older.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use the comparative with than: <span class=\"italic\">his house is larger than my house, this dress is more expensive than that one.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "A lot of people come to the Dead Sea to get healthier!  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It was quieter than you can imagine!  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I like the Dead Sea better than the Mediterranean Sea!", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "rose ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a light red-purple color", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: I want to paint my walls a rose color.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le05ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you need to review!", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "winding ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to twist or turn something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The vines were winding around the trees.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le05ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "sandstone", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a soft yellow or red rock often used as a building material ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Use sandstone to cut out blocks for the building.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le05ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "salty ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to taste or smell like salt ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Dead Sea is saltier than most lakes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le05ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "dense ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "thick; heavy ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Dead Sea water is dense as well.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le05ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to float ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to stay on the surface of the water", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: People can float on the surface of the Dead Sea.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le05ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "sea ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a large area of salt water ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The ship traveled by sea.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le05ob11aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "desert", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a large area of land covered in sand", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: They crossed the desert on a camel.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le05ob11aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Go online and look up the lyrics for the song \"Midnight at the Oasis\".", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a list of words you know and words you do not know.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look up words you do not know.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Listen to the song and read along.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I look up lyrics.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I list words I know and do not know.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use a dictionary to find words I do not know.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I listen to the song online.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn5le05ob11re2img06.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn5le05ob11re2img06.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Peter! Vanessa! <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Hey, Sally. Where did you go after we talked last? <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I went north to the Dead Sea. Then, I traveled east into the desert.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Are those places close?"}, {"image": "engenn5le05ob11re2img08.jpg", "time": "14000", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Jordan is next to both Egypt and Saudi Arabia.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: How was Petra?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: It was neat. I rode with some people through the winding rose-colored canyon. None of us spoke a word! It was quieter than you can imagine! It's amazing!"}, {"image": "engenn5le05ob11re2img05.jpg", "time": "31500", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: What about the Dead Sea? Do any people actually sink?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: No! The water is saltier and denser there. You just lie on it!<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I saw the picture of you covered in mud! Gross!<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: A lot of people think the mud makes them healthier! <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Could you send us more pictures? <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I'll attach some. I have plenty of new ones!"}], "audiosrc": "engenn5le05ob11re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le05ob11re2img06.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 2}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "I can say where places are in a country or city.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I ca